{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"batch_id\": \"audio_batch_06\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_e5ea4e366efdef35\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_e5ea4e366efdef35/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Audio artifact severity alignment\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_4d29a575cd8491bd99a586c4\", \"member_7b07aa5def81bd2c0a86511e\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor asks whether static noise is a major or minor artifact.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894026.000120\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894026.000120\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that one QA pass marks background static as major and another marks it as minor.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks both reviewers in the static thread to mark the exact defect timestamp and document their rating reasons if intelligibility remains intact.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"The team lead instructs the static thread to note artifact timestamps and whether speech remains intelligible so severity can be compared.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports a QA split on whether mild clipping should count as a major defect on AUDIO-7512.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor in the clipping thread reports audible clipping in the loudest phrase but says the words remain understandable.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897560.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897560.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"The same QA tutor who asks for details in the static thread asks in the clipping thread whether clipping obscures words or only briefly affects sound quality.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current instructions require assessment of intelligibility and the affected span: brief, localized clipping or static with clear speech is minor; an artifact making a material speech span unusable is major. Continuous artifacts or borderline impact require QA review with timestamps and an intelligibility description; duration alone does not establish a major defect.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:6eeb0c96\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ says to timestamp the affected clipping span and seek QA review of intelligibility and scope for continuous artifacts or unclear impact, rather than deciding from duration alone.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:e9bcf43a\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"Neither provided thread establishes a final artifact rating; the static thread ends with the team lead's request for timestamps and intelligibility information without a reply supplying those details, and the clipping thread ends with a QA tutor's question about impact on words.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894026.000120\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897560.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c11\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The September 24 calibration record records approval of a focused clipping calibration instead of rewriting the FAQ to make every continuous artifact major. Its recorded execution state is pending scheduling, with no booking, attendance or outcome recorded; it is not a standing rule and does not resolve later examples.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-clipping-calibration-approval@1.0:d0b0c638\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c12\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier calibration record describes A06-CAL-01 as a short audible pop with every word intelligible and A06-CAL-02 as repeated distortion across a phrase with disagreement about recoverable words. It calls for comparing affected spans and recoverable words, preserving the brief/intelligible minor example and holding any new threshold until the disputed recording is reviewed.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-clipping-calibration-approval@1.0:d0b0c638\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c13\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The October 2 batch announcement directs headphone use for the audio calibration exercise; it does not direct how to classify static or clipping.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790914912.000140:d54cf474\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two tutors report conflicting QA judgments about artifact severity: one for background static and one for mild clipping on AUDIO-7512.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Neither thread establishes a final rating; an earlier record shows a focused clipping calibration was approved, but scheduling and an outcome were not recorded.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894026.000120\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897560.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\", \"k:audio-clipping-calibration-approval@1.0:d0b0c638\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor asks whether static noise is a major or minor artifact.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894026.000120\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894026.000120\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor in the clipping thread reports audible clipping in the loudest phrase while the words remain understandable.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897560.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897560.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks both static reviewers for exact timestamps and rating reasons if intelligibility remains intact; in the clipping thread, the same QA tutor asks whether clipping obscures words or only briefly affects sound quality.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The team lead requests timestamps and an intelligibility description in the static thread, but the provided thread contains no reply supplying those details.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894026.000120\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897560.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d5\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"Current instructions distinguish brief, localized artifacts with clear speech from artifacts making a material speech span unusable, and require QA review for continuous artifacts or borderline impact.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:6eeb0c96\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d6\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The earlier calibration record pairs an intelligible short pop with disputed repeated distortion and preserves the existing minor-defect example rather than establishing a new threshold.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-clipping-calibration-approval@1.0:d0b0c638\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Schedule a short review session. Instruction: Check whether the approved clipping calibration has been booked or completed; if not, arrange it using the two recorded examples. Draft to copy: For the focused clipping calibration, please compare A06-CAL-01 and A06-CAL-02 by affected span and recoverable words.\\n\\nUse the current instructions:\\n- Brief, localized clipping or static with clear speech is minor.\\n- An artifact making a material speech span unusable is major.\\n- Continuous artifacts or borderline impact need QA review with timestamps and an intelligibility description; duration alone does not establish a major defect.\\n\\nKeep the existing brief/intelligible minor example. Hold any new threshold until the disputed recording is reviewed. This session does not by itself assign ratings to later reports. Scope: Arrange the previously approved session only if it has not already been booked or completed. Use current guidance, not the earlier rejected FAQ rewrite, and do not treat the session as resolving the static report or AUDIO-7512 in advance.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:6eeb0c96\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894026.000120\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897560.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\", \"k:audio-clipping-calibration-approval@1.0:d0b0c638\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c11\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c12\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The earlier approval supplies a focused way to compare disputed examples, and current guidance supplies the scoring rule. This addresses the unresolved QA disagreement without inventing a new threshold.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:6eeb0c96\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894026.000120\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897560.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\", \"k:audio-clipping-calibration-approval@1.0:d0b0c638\", \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:e9bcf43a\", \"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790914912.000140:d54cf474\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): Two tutors report conflicting QA severity judgments in separate threads without a final classification, while the earlier focused calibration has no recorded execution or outcome.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\", \"k:audio-clipping-calibration-approval@1.0:d0b0c638\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_4d29a575cd8491bd99a586c4\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_4d29a575cd8491bd99a586c4 is UNRESOLVED: The tutor's major-or-minor question receives requests for timestamps, intelligibility information and rating reasons, but no final classification.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894026.000120\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_7b07aa5def81bd2c0a86511e\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_7b07aa5def81bd2c0a86511e is UNRESOLVED: The tutor reports a QA split; a tutor describes understandable words, and a QA tutor asks about the clipping's impact without establishing a final classification.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897560.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity HIGH: Two distinct tutors report comparable QA scoring disagreements in separate threads during the same evening, indicating a labeling-consistency risk beyond one isolated question. This concerns the scoring disagreement, not the severity of either audio defect.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894026.000120\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897560.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:HIGH[3]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Multiple distinct people or affected tasks reporting a comparable problem within the relevant project, batch, and time window, suggesting broader disruption or systemic labeling risk. Consider the number affected relative to the known active group when that information is available; do not require an explicit statement of widespread impact\\\": A tutor reports major-versus-minor QA disagreement for background static, and a distinct tutor reports a QA split over whether mild clipping on AUDIO-7512 is major.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:recurrence\", \"kind\": \"HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE\", \"text\": \"Retrieved records show this problem occurred before.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-clipping-calibration-approval@1.0:d0b0c638\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U017\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U017 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U004\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U004 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894026.000120\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_4d29a575cd8491bd99a586c4\", \"thread_id\": \"1790894026.000120\", \"author_id\": \"U018\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T22:33:46.000120Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U018\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Is static noise a major artifact or minor?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894072.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_4d29a575cd8491bd99a586c4\", \"thread_id\": \"1790894026.000120\", \"author_id\": \"U017\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T22:34:32.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U018\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"One QA pass marks this background static as major, another as minor.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894125.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_4d29a575cd8491bd99a586c4\", \"thread_id\": \"1790894026.000120\", \"author_id\": \"U007\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T22:35:25.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U018\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Can both reviewers mark the exact timestamp where the defect occurs? If intelligibility remains intact, document why the artifact rating was chosen.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790894163.000339\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_4d29a575cd8491bd99a586c4\", \"thread_id\": \"1790894026.000120\", \"author_id\": \"U006\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T22:36:03.000339Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U018\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Please note the artifact timestamps and whether speech remains intelligible; otherwise we cannot calibrate severity.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897512.000121\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_7b07aa5def81bd2c0a86511e\", \"thread_id\": \"1790897512.000121\", \"author_id\": \"U004\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T23:31:52.000121Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U004\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"QA split on whether mild clipping should count as a major defect. (task ref AUDIO-7512)\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897560.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_7b07aa5def81bd2c0a86511e\", \"thread_id\": \"1790897512.000121\", \"author_id\": \"U010\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T23:32:40.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U004\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"The clipping is audible in the loudest phrase, but I can still understand the words.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790897607.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_7b07aa5def81bd2c0a86511e\", \"thread_id\": \"1790897512.000121\", \"author_id\": \"U007\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T23:33:27.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U004\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Does the clipping obscure words or only briefly affect sound quality?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:6eeb0c96\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — Instructions (v1.3)\", \"sections\": [\"Scoring audio quality\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Scoring audio quality\\n- Assess intelligibility and the affected span, not the word “clipping” alone.\\n- Brief, localized clipping or static with speech remaining clear is a minor defect.\\n- An artifact that makes a material speech span unusable is a major defect.\\n- Continuous artifacts or borderline impact require QA review with timestamps and an intelligibility description. Duration alone does not establish a major defect.\\n- Before treating silence as a content issue, verify playback, volume, and whether the audio file itself is silent. Preserve uncertainty when this cannot be checked.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1131a168\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — Instructions (v1.3)\", \"sections\": [\"Content-quality rubric\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Content-quality rubric\\nMajor/minor here describe task-quality defects, not operational incident severity.\\n\\n| Dimension | Major defect | Minor defect | Acceptable / no automatic penalty |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Intelligibility | A material speech span is unusable | Brief clipping/static with words still clear | Background variation that does not impair the task |\\n| Audio–transcript correspondence | Key content is missing or contradicted | A limited omission that does not change meaning | Equivalent wording where the task allows it |\\n| Language match | A substantial unrequested mismatch with the required language | A limited genuine mismatch affecting adherence | Permitted switching, ordinary loanwords, or an acceptable accent |\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:e9bcf43a\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Scoring\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-20T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-20T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Scoring\\n\\n### Q: How should I score mild clipping?\\nBrief, localized clipping with clear speech is a minor defect. Timestamp the affected span. For continuous artifacts or unclear impact, ask QA to review intelligibility and scope; do not decide from duration alone.\\n\\n### Q: The transcript and audio disagree. What do I do?\\nRecord the exact mismatch as a correspondence issue. Distinguish a recording error from a reference-transcript error; do not classify the mismatch as a playback failure.\\n\\n### Q: How much speaker overlap is allowed before the transcription fails?\\nMark the overlapping or unintelligible interval and preserve the usable remainder. Timestamp the span. Do not infer a whole-clip failure from a short affected interval.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790914912.000140:d54cf474\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"title\": \"Slack announcement in audio-multimodal-announcements at 2026-10-02T04:21:52.000140+00:00\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1790914912.000140\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1790914912.000140\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-10-02T04:21:52.000140+00:00\", \"basis\": \"created_at\", \"created_at\": \"2026-10-02T04:21:52.000140+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"batch_id\": \"audio_batch_06\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"UNKNOWN\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U006\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-10-02T04:21:52.000140+00:00 by TEAM_LEAD (audio_batch_06): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nReminder to use headphones for the audio calibration exercise.\\n\\nContext reply [1790914961.000113] by U017 (TUTOR):\\nThanks, I’ll review the examples before calibration.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:3a08035c\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — Instructions (v1.3)\", \"sections\": [\"Tool incidents and submission\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Tool incidents and submission\\n| Incident | Required handling |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Playback unavailable | Report task ID and reproduction details; leave content quality unassessed |\\n| Intermittent playback | Record the affected tasks and whether access returned; do not assume every task recovered |\\n| Submit disabled or click fails | Capture task ID, required-field state, error and button behavior |\\n| Confirmation delayed | Check the actual receipt before recording submission as complete |\\n\\nTool incidents are assessed separately under the operational severity rubric. A selected rating or successful reload is not proof that the original task was submitted.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-clipping-calibration-approval@1.0:d0b0c638\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-clipping-calibration-approval@1.0\", \"title\": \"Approve a focused clipping calibration\", \"sections\": [\"Review context\"